Slicing a string literal ("abc"[:]) emits invalid LLVM: extractvalue is applied
to the i8* string-constant pointer instead of a %BnSlice aggregate.  genSliceExpr
(pkg/binate/ir/gen_access.bn) only array-to-slice-converts a TYP_ARRAY collection;
a string literal's genExpr yields a bare i8* CONST_STRING that misses that arm.
Fails in every mode (a codegen bug, not mode-specific).  Tracked in
explorations/claude-todo.md.
